## 5. Biological Reference Numbers

### Human vs. rat neuron counts by region

|Brain Region|Human|Rat|Note|
|---|---|---|---|
|Cerebral Cortex (total)|~16 billion|~21 million|Human cortex is folded (gyrencephalic); rat cortex is smooth|
|Frontal/Prefrontal Cortex|~3.5–4.5 billion|~3–4 million|Humans devote far more cortex to executive function|
|Visual/Auditory/Sensory Cortex|~6–7 billion|~8–10 million|Rats lean on whisker/barrel cortex + olfaction|
|Hippocampus (both hemispheres)|~30–40 million|~1.2–2 million|Proportionally larger in rats (spatial navigation)|
|Cerebellum|~69 billion|~130 million|~80% of all neurons in both species|
|Olfactory Bulb|~10 million|~25–30 million|Rats have _more_ neurons here than humans|
|Brainstem/Subcortical|~700 million|~15–20 million|Basic survival functions|
|**Total**|**~86 billion**|**~200 million**|Humans: ~430× more neurons|
|Glia (non-neuronal)|~84 billion (~1:1 w/ neurons)|~130 million|—|

### Neuron count vs. achievable FPGA scale (illustrative only — see §7 caveats)

|Organism|Approx. Neurons|Comparable Config (by count only)|
|---|---|---|
|_C. elegans_ (roundworm)|302|~3 chunks, any config|
|Tardigrade|~200|~2 chunks|
|Jellyfish (Hydra)|~5,000|~50 chunks|
|Fruit fly|~135,000|Cyclone V v3–v6 on-chip range|
|Ant|~250,000|Template/mask model on Cyclone V|
|Honeybee|~1,000,000|Versal on-chip range|
|Mouse|~70,000,000|Between Cyclone V+DDR3 and Versal+LPDDR5X|
|Rat|~200,000,000|Cyclone V + DDR3 (streamed, ~1.6 Hz)|
|Cat|~1,000,000,000|Versal + LPDDR5X range|
|Human|~86,000,000,000|Far beyond any single-board config described here|

---

## 6. Biological Neuron vs. LLM "Neuron"

- **Biological neuron:** dendrites collect chemical signals → soma sums excitatory/inhibitory charge → if it crosses a voltage threshold (~-55 mV) at the axon hillock, it fires an all-or-nothing action potential ("spike") down the axon.
- **Binary or not?** Both. The _spike itself_ is strictly binary (fires or doesn't, always the same height). But information is encoded in a _non-binary_ way through **spike rate/frequency** and **timing**, plus continuously-variable synaptic (connection) strength.
- **LLM "neuron":** a mathematical unit computing a weighted sum + nonlinearity, part of a static matrix multiplication. It doesn't fire "over time" the way a biological or spiking neuron does — it's evaluated once per forward pass.
- **This project's neuron:** closer to the biological spiking model (all-or-nothing fire on threshold/overflow) than to an LLM unit, but far simpler than either — no continuous synaptic weights, no learned embeddings, no gradient-based credit assignment.

---

## 7. This System vs. Conway's Game of Life vs. LLM

|Feature|Conway's Game of Life|Traditional LLM|This System|
|---|---|---|---|
|Basic unit|Cell (alive/dead)|Vector / token weight|Neuron (`N`)|
|Layout|2D spatial grid|Deep unfolded layers|Spatial grids (`C`)|
|Rules|Fixed local neighbor checks|Global matrix multiplication|Dynamic cardinal mask (`M`)|
|Trigger|Living neighbor count (2 or 3)|Math activation functions|Accumulator overflow (`A`)|
|Time|Discrete clock steps|Static feed-forward pass|Event-driven clock cycles|
|Learning|None (fixed rules)|Gradient descent / backprop|GA bit-flip mutation|

This is genuinely a reasonable way to describe the project: it's an **evolvable cellular automaton with sparse neural routing** — a digital ecosystem, not a super-calculator. It won't pass a Turing test out of the box, because it isn't built on language data or gradient-trained representations; it's built to simulate the emergent, physically-constrained dynamics of biological tissue.

---

## 8. Proposed Language-Learning Curriculum (as designed)

|Phase|Goal|Estimated Time (as originally proposed)|
|---|---|---|
|1 — Signal grounding|ASCII in → memory echo → main brain → ASCII out, 95% repetition on a single character|Hours to 1–2 days|
|2 — Short sequences|Reliably reproduce 2–5 letter words (CAT, HAT, SAT)|1–3 weeks|
|3 — Basic syntax|Recognize/complete kindergarten-level sentences ("the cat sat on the hat")|1–3+ months|

**Named bottlenecks:**

- **Fitness-function bottleneck** — if the evaluator runs on a host PC over UART/JTAG, data transfer speed (not the FPGA itself) becomes the limiting factor.
- **Fitness cascades** — a mutation that helps a later stage (e.g. 2-letter recognition) can silently break an earlier one (1-letter recognition) unless earlier pathways are frozen/locked before moving on.

---

## 10. Open Questions / Next Steps

- [ ] Decide: pursue the 46-bit custom-wiring model (higher per-neuron expressiveness, ~108K neurons) or the cardinal-mask/template model (lower per-neuron expressiveness, ~400K+ neurons)?
- [ ] Build the automated training harness _on_ the FPGA (avoid host-PC UART bottleneck for fitness evaluation)
- [ ] Prototype `C_HIP` / `C_CTX` / `C_IO` regional chunk sizing before committing to a fixed layout
- [ ] Define the refractory/inhibitory/decay parameters concretely (values, not just mechanisms)
- [ ] Decide on a realistic, scoped success criterion (e.g. "stable emergent wave patterns," "reliable byte-recall memory chunk") before attempting full sentence-level language

